{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>Va-yichad.</b> Rashi explained: his flesh broke out in goose-pimples, etc. And Rabenu Tam said he found support for the matter according to Rashi's explanation in 'and Yarha, and he gave his daughter to Yarha his servant as a wife.' Reckon thirteen [generations] from Yarha the servant of Sheshan to Elishama, and expound from this verse ״ישמעאל בן נתניה בן אלישמע״ — that he was of the Nethinim. From here [we learn] regarding a convert who reverted to his former ways: up to fourteen generations, that he was shedding blood and doing the deed of an Aramean. And three generations he does not count, because an Egyptian convert is not a [valid] convert until three generations, and from there onward you find ten generations."], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The phrase 'and Yarha, and he gave his daughter to Yarha his servant as a wife' refers to 1 Chronicles 2:34–35, where Sheshan gives his daughter to his Egyptian servant Yarha; the genealogical chain there runs from Yarha to Elishama. The comment links this to Gedaliah's assassin Ishmael ben Netanyah ben Elishama (2 Kings 25:23, Jeremiah 40:8), tracing him back to the Egyptian servant Yarha."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:26.213384795Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}